em "What is the $y$-intercept of $y=-5{e}^{-{x}^{3}}+3?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-5{e}^{-(0)^{3}}+3 \\\\  & =-5{e}^{0}+3 \\\\  & =-5(1)+3 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-92930/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7df2ec3-6138-5b84-864b-a856c28b9747"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-92930"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-92929/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "ec9be228-b251-53db-9abf-16e69436d6da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92929/selection/24b264e72b26a1586a9a779172cdc62569680a48e8e1da6fe0efb3117c552b0b" :answer/id #uuid "1b4295bd-4edf-5d0c-a99f-aa3651f283be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{101}{100}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92929/selection/012adbeb2791efced32a5fbabcc0132d6c4ea07a7e9ecb743b97a66d903cc6b6" :answer/id #uuid "3cd8a0c9-4752-5dbc-9ef5-1eb6be87880b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92929/selection/8321a2979a16551077c65e6e38879453e2008e1e6ec20a58ad319189f2ffe86d" :answer/id #uuid "269e75eb-b53c-5d4a-ae29-05fbc52afcb9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "There is no $y$-intercept" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92929/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "222fe4e0-5900-52cd-894b-49747b216c5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92929/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e1a0e3-8424-554e-851b-6a1d37bb03ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-92929/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-92929/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-92929/selection/24b264e72b26a1586a9a779172cdc62569680a48e8e1da6fe0efb3117c552b0b" "q-92929/selection/012adbeb2791efced32a5fbabcc0132d6c4ea07a7e9ecb743b97a66d903cc6b6" "q-92929/selection/8321a2979a16551077c65e6e38879453e2008e1e6ec20a58ad319189f2ffe86d" "q-92929/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-92929" :question/id #uuid "1ac0fce3-540d-53f6-ae4b-b41d1a5a4d86" :question/math-academy-id "q-92929" :question/problem "Determine the $y$-intercept of $y={(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2x}+1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the $y$-intercept, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={(\\frac{1}{10})}^{2(0)}+1 \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{10})}^{0}+1 \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-92929/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7df2ec3-6138-5b84-864b-a856c28b9747"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-92929"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40799/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "cef578bd-2d74-5385-938d-8d34be1e59a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40799/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "e3a9ef1a-73bd-50f4-9852-cc8cdb8812eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40799/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ebe2f501-1459-5766-8be9-048735e51c1c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40799/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "b386b797-7dd0-51f1-967b-7999c28d40ad" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40799/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "335ae99e-157a-5998-8a27-132ed22d933b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40799/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "391ead5f-b789-5d3f-a780-f386561cfd8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40799/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-40799/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-40799/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-40799/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-40799/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-40799/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40799" :question/id #uuid "dee8af6a-2a0f-5055-b4c5-db0b64915d01" :question/math-academy-id "q-40799" :question/problem "Which of the following values ​are possible outputs of $f(x)=-{(2)}^{-x}?$\n\n- $0$\n- $0.5$\n- $-0.5$" :question/worked-solution "The range of ${2}^{-x}$ is\n\n$$\n{2}^{-x}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-1$ yields the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1){(2)}^{-x} & <0 \\\\ -{(2)}^{-x} & <0 \\\\ f(x) & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)<0.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=-0.5$ is an output of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943819/assets/95ad3043259402375e7b5822aef88d77027222a3372c2b8ab042d1b54e08666f.png)\n\n \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-40799/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef75bc93-76da-5992-8285-181b808eb7a0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40799"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40798/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "1dc45671-fcf7-5dbd-a6f5-ad7bbe7bade5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40798/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "08f0ce87-d050-5e19-957a-5e5510d9d990" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40798/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "6013cc77-c04f-55ca-9423-ddc9a30cb189" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40798/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "3d7ca28c-b905-56f5-97f2-bc4b2bd63e4a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40798/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "a9d8bb8f-3583-598a-ac0c-fe8ece92b8f6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40798/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "15e3218f-83b0-52cf-8efc-68875e84a8e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40798/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-40798/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-40798/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-40798/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-40798/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-40798/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40798" :question/id #uuid "9be6186b-78c0-5e07-9888-65f5a8e9a495" :question/math-academy-id "q-40798" :question/problem "Which of the following values ​are possible outputs of  $f(x)={(1.5)}^{2x}-0.5?$ \n\n- $0$\n- $-0.2$\n- $-0.8$" :question/worked-solution "The range of ${(1.5)}^{x}$ is\n\n$$\n{(1.5)}^{x}>0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{(1.5)}^{2x}>0.\n$$\n\nSubtracting  $0.5$ from the above inequality yields the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1.5)}^{2x} & >0 \\\\ {(1.5)}^{2x}-0.5 & >0-0.5 \\\\ f(x) & >-0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)>-0.5.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=0$ and $y=-0.2$ are outputs of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943819/assets/5876d2095bfd91417d2e6395f8a02ae817ebd476076bae929d79709ea7961a3e.png)\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-40798/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef75bc93-76da-5992-8285-181b808eb7a0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40798"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40556/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "861770e4-c455-50cf-87d1-31c8a7efd95e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40556/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "e32709e1-f9be-5b82-9f76-d731a0120ecd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40556/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "215ea77d-df2f-5ca6-ae93-331ed95a28a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40556/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "ea4f7e3f-279b-5854-b258-f9e5a8129984" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40556/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "18d3f191-98dd-52c2-9ae0-9f3920c7e43a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40556/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfa503d1-0f78-5c68-be51-da15744d2f9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40556/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-40556/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-40556/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-40556/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-40556/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-40556/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40556" :question/id #uuid "a8f42f9f-1668-5edc-b773-eb09cabbd64b" :question/math-academy-id "q-40556" :question/problem "Which of the following values ​are possible outputs of $f(x)=-5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1}+3?$\n\n- $-3$\n- $2$\n- $10$" :question/worked-solution "The range of ${(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}$ is\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x}>0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-5$ and then adding $3,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1} & >0 \\\\ -5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1} & <0 \\\\ -5{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{x-1}+3 & <0+3 \\\\ f(x) & <3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)<3.$ Thus, of the given values, only $y=-3$ and $y=2$ are  outputs of $y=f(x).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943819/assets/b220b9c53bfaa49fe9b1b1c70fb9e21d08e247f44df8716846d08fd37ac2cf11.png)\n\n  \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-40556/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef75bc93-76da-5992-8285-181b808eb7a0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-165973/selection/b4bfb76aa4e9c4781d088ea715d963425a8d7fdef5ce0b19a20709d1c2573334" :answer/id #uuid "97c5412c-33e7-5456-bea1-47e85c6cdcb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165973/selection/1d3044757d46acdb3acefa381c6147d4c162f26434588e833e8c1aed29141e20" :answer/id #uuid "31939db6-a7a9-5f45-9ab5-1402ddc0c6d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\in (-3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165973/selection/fda91539099e3ba5d904487e67f5e64671524312a45a4de9ae1dedf5627bccd1" :answer/id #uuid "a06172b2-f368-5bf3-9a97-353158d0113b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165973/selection/5555f6e81d232920c34fe65605fee25597493cef9296d2f9f9072fe03d77a8d8" :answer/id #uuid "ea483945-526f-5e91-8b8d-6b294b4384f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,3]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165973/selection/e7f85129ab79b6f3f7e04828ceb597aef77aaa79c0ddc1af2130832060db1d1a" :answer/id #uuid "dbb26809-881f-59cd-9ad7-6ccdbd4919b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\in [-3,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-165973/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b06c741f-03c4-5bc3-b824-7edd41c8c947" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-165973/selection/1d3044757d46acdb3acefa381c6147d4c162f26434588e833e8c1aed29141e20" :answer-field/choices ["q-165973/selection/b4bfb76aa4e9c4781d088ea715d963425a8d7fdef5ce0b19a20709d1c2573334" "q-165973/selection/1d3044757d46acdb3acefa381c6147d4c162f26434588e833e8c1aed29141e20" "q-165973/selection/fda91539099e3ba5d904487e67f5e64671524312a45a4de9ae1dedf5627bccd1" "q-165973/selection/5555f6e81d232920c34fe65605fee25597493cef9296d2f9f9072fe03d77a8d8" "q-165973/selection/e7f85129ab79b6f3f7e04828ceb597aef77aaa79c0ddc1af2130832060db1d1a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-165973" :question/id #uuid "3b1c999f-be1d-51d5-bb01-040649089426" :question/math-academy-id "q-165973" :question/problem "What is the range of $y=2(5)^{x}-3?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of ${5}^{x}$ is\n\n$$\n{5}^{x}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $2$ and then subtracting $3,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x} & >0 \\\\ 2(5)^{x} & >0 \\\\ 2(5)^{x}-3 & >0-3 \\\\ y & >-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in (-3,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $f(x)=2(5)^{x}-3$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943819/assets/c8179a12c8032d81ebbdb8a5a95c158e905fab4d24aa68f0eeef1f4bc4971a0b.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-165973/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef75bc93-76da-5992-8285-181b808eb7a0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-165973"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40392/selection/d12d1f4ec78209a9fa9a5d3866e00071ac5379804efe604b5932cbde52ae8415" :answer/id #uuid "85c9da1b-b455-561c-848f-9cf1f61b9610" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\in (-1,+\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40392/selection/a50bea7ec206e19cf5971017612cd38e8580c0510ae1edb218ba8da6af716114" :answer/id #uuid "6233f435-ecaa-5f75-9856-c9ff32da0583" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,-1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40392/selection/7975541ab26842137d40a49ad83a31bf4a2d6eaeef0da69cb0171b2ae7dc9def" :answer/id #uuid "0c5c758e-51ba-554f-b5e2-4bd1bd65893b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\in (1,+\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40392/selection/ff1756c4e7b2c74c3ee0ed2435044bb99ac978b8a2a9be74e1b898693cd0b888" :answer/id #uuid "ca21d80c-be11-5535-bcad-ad8097238fce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40392/selection/5424f8ef96d95460ba035c99b00252102f6e9bd1ef251b71193053354bfce0c3" :answer/id #uuid "96c36916-a109-55b8-93cd-1751ba74c634" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\in (-\\infty ,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40392/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "91f58415-3af7-5158-bb7c-c3a5e5fdda97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40392/selection/ff1756c4e7b2c74c3ee0ed2435044bb99ac978b8a2a9be74e1b898693cd0b888" :answer-field/choices ["q-40392/selection/d12d1f4ec78209a9fa9a5d3866e00071ac5379804efe604b5932cbde52ae8415" "q-40392/selection/a50bea7ec206e19cf5971017612cd38e8580c0510ae1edb218ba8da6af716114" "q-40392/selection/7975541ab26842137d40a49ad83a31bf4a2d6eaeef0da69cb0171b2ae7dc9def" "q-40392/selection/ff1756c4e7b2c74c3ee0ed2435044bb99ac978b8a2a9be74e1b898693cd0b888" "q-40392/selection/5424f8ef96d95460ba035c99b00252102f6e9bd1ef251b71193053354bfce0c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40392" :question/id #uuid "0ba8974b-b12d-5e2d-8293-45498541a65b" :question/math-academy-id "q-40392" :question/problem "What is the range of $y=-3(2)^{2-x}-1?$" :question/worked-solution "The range of ${2}^{-x}$ is \n\n$$\n{2}^{-x}>0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{2}^{2-x}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-3$ and then subtracting $1,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{2-x} & >0 \\\\ -3(2)^{2-x} & <0 \\\\ -3(2)^{2-x}-1 & <0-1 \\\\ y & <-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1).$ \n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $f(x)=-3(2)^{2-x}-1$ is shown below.  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943819/assets/88b75fabc306eb09a7ca63c909de3272cc776bf808e29da4cc08ae2c5a53e192.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40392/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef75bc93-76da-5992-8285-181b808eb7a0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40392"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-66674/selection/f3ea0285f3406636be894fd7cffb98ae0739aed6ed85196fb79469657d0fb7c6" :answer/id #uuid "5d6f65f1-e642-5f21-ae3c-aa3ba49bac01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{log}_{2}⁡(4)-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66674/selection/3985991540ce71965b5922eadb9de27d1ab0c464fbd427fa714285d00bb96e31" :answer/id #uuid "fa29ff71-10ca-584c-8acf-dacb25f21e68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{log}_{2}⁡(3)-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66674/selection/b69cc2d6c0a4197dafd8dfed2ab9e81ace66c988f0e30727b11a2ffa9358d0bb" :answer/id #uuid "d00fc6bd-5e17-57c4-82d3-32343022514c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4{log}_{2}⁡(3)+4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66674/selection/4b9e205eeb3f3dfd2490a0a17d651ffaf2dc8e187633ac3d7ebe3878ee290e2a" :answer/id #uuid "6a6bb87f-b4f8-56b7-b489-2ab782e1657d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3{log}_{2}⁡(4)-1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66674/selection/1cc1ae631fdd24b6274e20eaa7dac83a80fc45507eb86c56dc6adbeeacbcdfce" :answer/id #uuid "4c44378a-10aa-52b7-af56-50fc331fee6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{log}_{2}⁡(3)+2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-66674/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9548eed4-7115-5977-a19f-cb5bbc5a395a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-66674/selection/b69cc2d6c0a4197dafd8dfed2ab9e81ace66c988f0e30727b11a2ffa9358d0bb" :answer-field/choices ["q-66674/selection/f3ea0285f3406636be894fd7cffb98ae0739aed6ed85196fb79469657d0fb7c6" "q-66674/selection/3985991540ce71965b5922eadb9de27d1ab0c464fbd427fa714285d00bb96e31" "q-66674/selection/b69cc2d6c0a4197dafd8dfed2ab9e81ace66c988f0e30727b11a2ffa9358d0bb" "q-66674/selection/4b9e205eeb3f3dfd2490a0a17d651ffaf2dc8e187633ac3d7ebe3878ee290e2a" "q-66674/selection/1cc1ae631fdd24b6274e20eaa7dac83a80fc45507eb86c56dc6adbeeacbcdfce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-66674" :question/id #uuid "62b31fbf-15a4-5f0d-9c03-266e00a60703" :question/math-academy-id "q-66674" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=-{2}^{3x-4}+81.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-{2}^{3x-4}+81=0\n$$\n\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by subtracting $81$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{2}^{3x-4}+81 & =0 \\\\ -{2}^{3x-4}+\\cancel{81}-\\cancel{81} & =0-81 \\\\ -{2}^{3x-4} & =-81 \\\\ {2}^{3x-4} & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite $81$ as ${3}^{4}$ to get\n\n$$\n{2}^{3x-4}={3}^{4}.\n$$\n\nThen we take ${log}_{2}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{3x-4} & ={3}^{4} \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡({2}^{3x-4}) & ={log}_{2}⁡({3}^{4}) \\\\ 3x-4 & =4{log}_{2}⁡(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-4 & =4{log}_{2}⁡(3) \\\\ 3x & =4{log}_{2}⁡(3)+4 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4{log}_{2}⁡(3)+4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-66674/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee02c223-dd7f-5c5d-b09f-e7bc6bd16b0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-66674"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-92995/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "9872287a-d14b-572e-b283-a073b595b927" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92995/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "8819b3ba-cf8b-5860-b897-e8e0c51668e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92995/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "4efff487-16cb-59f5-87e5-4bfe5cb45662" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92995/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "e339b207-78ee-50fa-b0cb-06d77b8ea048" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92995/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b2473fab-db0b-5ba0-817f-c33a6f9c697f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92995/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cfa08790-b879-579a-a81f-5cf216affe71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-92995/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-92995/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-92995/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-92995/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-92995/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-92995/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-92995" :question/id #uuid "f6bb98f4-14ff-5456-8b32-1fb3e17bc5b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-92995" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)={e}^{x}-{e}^{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n{e}^{x}-{e}^{4}=0\n$$\n\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by adding ${e}^{4}$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{x}-{e}^{4} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}-\\cancel{{e}^{4}}+\\cancel{{e}^{4}} & =0+{e}^{4} \\\\ {e}^{x} & ={e}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $e$, we equate the exponents. This gives\n\n$$\nx=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-92995/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee02c223-dd7f-5c5d-b09f-e7bc6bd16b0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-92995"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93000/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "6b55e90c-4cba-5c40-a2f2-87e034c50df0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93000/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "542cc09b-b9e2-56a9-8c38-b618e006ac6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93000/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "8eea48af-6294-5306-95c6-a4b5d8fe9d5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93000/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "c8af98a8-a5da-5ef4-954a-fa8c6e8a8995" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93000/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "769bd808-4940-5dc2-8e70-4cb9b444587d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93000/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2611de0-f2bd-5f2a-b92f-3ca250a6e87e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93000/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-93000/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-93000/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-93000/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-93000/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-93000/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93000" :question/id #uuid "dfe344bf-34e4-55e9-b8e1-a7b9ffb4f282" :question/math-academy-id "q-93000" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=-15{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{x-1}+10.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-15{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{x-1}+10=0\n$$\n\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by subtracting $10$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-15{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{x-1}+10 & =0 \\\\ -15{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{x-1}+\\cancel{10}-\\cancel{10} & =0-10 \\\\ -15{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{x-1} & =-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $-15,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-15{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{x-1} & =-10 \\\\ {(\\frac{3}{2})}^{x-1} & =\\frac{10}{15} \\\\ {(\\frac{3}{2})}^{x-1} & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite $\\frac{2}{3}$ as ${(\\frac{3}{2})}^{-1}$ to get\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{x-1}={(\\frac{3}{2})}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since both sides of the equation share the same base $(\\frac{3}{2})$, we equate the exponents. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-1 & =-1 \\\\ x & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93000/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee02c223-dd7f-5c5d-b09f-e7bc6bd16b0c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93000"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-92998/selection/579a455fd4c27a20d4aa8a7ff34b566cebf8afb8bcb3d385a715cad8c4bac8d5" :answer/id #uuid "aff65057-e752-5d86-a8d7-29ab66bcb91a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92998/selection/b256ebadf6977b5de98e4043194c2ea7d466de6a93d39ec358a8217a23cf4518" :answer/id #uuid "1b2d2fd1-765b-5f2f-bd4d-e98802629809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92998/selection/a4e81ef6d429b1d32467a2fa1b60c694efab6a4e9d44758c8205854de40f9616" :answer/id #uuid "ca1a10dc-ece8-5f93-bbfd-2798c9d2c2c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92998/selection/32e93dc7a0bf0f72d87de9702227810ce5b55d9f88a260f535687ec057d0851c" :answer/id #uuid "4aa962d8-2359-5b0b-bc47-6962a02a3d51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)-1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92998/selection/ffec377e8d5f7c5eefde25b2666e234876d4c2601aaabd9c1f869f0e76c68d5c" :answer/id #uuid "fec070c8-59e3-58f6-a7aa-62488f62c58a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-92998/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1a89f27-0e4d-5982-b3d8-98c60e5f4cca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-92998/selection/579a455fd4c27a20d4aa8a7ff34b566cebf8afb8bcb3d385a715cad8c4bac8d5" :answer-field/choices ["q-92998/selection/579a455fd4c27a20d4aa8a7ff34b566cebf8afb8bcb3d385a715cad8c4bac8d5" "q-92998/selection/b256ebadf6977b5de98e4043194c2ea7d466de6a93d39ec358a8217a23cf4518" "q-92998/selection/a4e81ef6d429b1d32467a2fa1b60c694efab6a4e9d44758c8205854de40f9616" "q-92998/selection/32e93dc7a0bf0f72d87de9702227810ce5b55d9f88a260f535687ec057d0851c" "q-92998/selection/ffec377e8d5f7c5eefde25b2666e234876d4c2601aaabd9c1f869f0e76c68d5c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-92998" :question/id #uuid "bee910a5-bfec-5da0-b294-9b388e560648" :question/math-academy-id "q-92998" :question/problem "Find the root of $f(x)=4{e}^{2x-1}-8.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n4{e}^{2x-1}-8=0\n$$\n\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by adding $8$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{2x-1}-8 & =0 \\\\ 4{e}^{2x-1}-\\cancel{8}+\\cancel{8} & =0+8 \\\\ 4{e}^{2x-1} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{e}^{2x-1} & =8 \\\\ {e}^{2x-1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2x-1} & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x-1}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 2x-1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\ 2x & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-92998/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee02c223-dd7f-5c5d-b09f-e7